    "description": "I work on the Core UEFI team developing secure and robust system firmware in C and Rust. Our work spans across UEFI, architectural FW, the OS, and the platform. We drive industry security initiatives and work closely with the open source community and OEMs. We are driving best of class practices in the FW space (typically absent): unit testing, integration testing, functional testing, memory protections, code reusability, and more. We are driving investments into FW developed in Rust, leveraging not just the safety guarantees of the language, but more importantly the opportunity to revisit outdated code patterns and rewrite them in safe ways.",
